{"type":"message","message":{"id":"gen-1775345269-gb0ZkVvHpBynnGoGNF7K","role":"assistant","created":1775345285,"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Hmm, that doesn't look right either. Looking at the original data again, those numbers look like they're for \"Individual income taxes\" not Social Security Administration. Let me look at the raw HTML more carefully.\n\nLooking at the original extract again:\n```\n<tr><td>Social Security Administration</td><td>155,304</td><td>10</td><td>628,880</td><td>784,194</td><td>70,743</td><td>16</td><td>683,420</td><td>754,179</td></tr>\n```\n\nSo we have:\n- General funds (1): 155,304\n- Management, consolidated, revolving and special funds (2): 10\n- Trust funds (3): 628,880\n- Total funds (4): 784,194 (this is FY2011)\n- General funds (5): 70,743\n- Management, consolidated, revolving and special funds (6): 16\n- Trust funds (7): 683,420\n- Total funds (8): 754,179 (this is FY2010)\n\nThe issue is my regex was picking up the wrong values. Let me try a different approach - the SSA row should have values in the hundreds of millions for total funds, not in the trillions.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_16c8740223474559b76d90fa","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"python3 << 'EOF'\nimport re\n\n# The SSA row structure is:\n# <tr><td>Social Security Administration</td><td>155,304</td><td>10</td><td>628,880</td><td>784,194</td><td>70,743</td><td>16</td><td>683,420</td><td>754,179</td></tr>\n# We need the 4th and 8th <td> values (index 3 and 7 in 0-indexed)\n\ndef extract_ssa_from_file(filepath):\n    with open(filepath, 'r') as f:\n        content = f.read()\n    \n    # Find the row with Social Security Administration\n    # The row has format: <tr><td>Social Security Administration</td>...\n    pattern = r'<tr><td>Social Security Administration</td>(.*?)</tr>'\n    match = re.search(pattern, content)\n    if match:\n        row_content = match.group(1)\n        # Extract all td values\n        tds = re.findall(r'<td>([^<]+)</td>', row_content)\n        print(f\"  Found {len(tds)} td elements: {tds}\")\n        if len(tds) >= 8:\n            # Column 4 (index 3) = This fiscal year to date Total\n            # Column 8 (index 7) = Prior fiscal year to date Total\n            current_fy_total = tds[3].replace(',', '')\n            prior_fy_total = tds[7].replace(',', '')\n            return int(current_fy_total), int(prior_fy_total)\n    return None, None\n\nprint(\"Extracting SSA outlay values from FFO-4 tables:\\n\")\n\nfiles = [\n    ('/app/resources/treasury_bulletin_2011_12_page_25.txt', 'Dec 2011'),\n    ('/app/resources/treasury_bulletin_2013_12_page_24.txt', 'Dec 2013'),\n    ('/app/resources/treasury_bulletin_2015_12_page_23.txt', 'Dec 2015'),\n    ('/app/resources/treasury_bulletin_2017_12_page_23.txt', 'Dec 2017'),\n    ('/app/resources/treasury_bulletin_2019_12_page_22.txt', 'Dec 2019'),\n]\n\ndata_dict = {}\nfor filepath, label in files:\n    current, prior = extract_ssa_from_file(filepath)\n    print(f\"{label}: Current FY (col4) = {current}, Prior FY (col8) = {prior}\")\n    # Extract FY year from label\n    year = int(label.split()[1])\n    data_dict[year] = current      # This fiscal year = current FY\n    data_dict[year - 1] = prior    # Prior fiscal year\n\nprint(\"\\n\\nData by FY:\")\nfor fy in sorted(data_dict.keys()):\n    print(f\"FY{fy}: {data_dict[fy]:,}\")\nEOF"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
